{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"The file /Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-cledger-push-scope.md has been updated successfully.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01VtW4uPUixrrSZt2YZorddj","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","dirty_fingerprint":"bbe20560a71a254635cbd033aa353a00fbd2c3fb094525003f36b4423871768b","head":"c841d5d76d898a65f06312edfc538793eb0bdb61","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295","seq":1386},"id":"ev1-ba1318a5384779346fdb6e227b1407beb0bdf343b65351c1a48b8001bc4227be","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-29T04:34:13.759Z","producer":{"session_id":"cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.220","tool":"cledger","version":"0.15.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"The file /Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-cledger-push-scope.md has been updated successfully.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01VtW4uPUixrrSZt2YZorddj","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"parentUuid":"e07b5cd3-229f-4e8d-8b1e-cfc07e840319","promptId":"aef76774-5950-4839-81d4-564d30bdec59","sessionId":"cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295","sessionKind":"bg","session_id":"cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295","slug":"temporal-coalescing-peacock","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e07b5cd3-229f-4e8d-8b1e-cfc07e840319","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:34:13.759Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-cledger-push-scope.md","memdirStamped":true,"newString":"**0.15.0:** the hook now passes git's pre-push stdin through, so scope follows\nthe refs actually being pushed (local shas; deletions skipped; multi-ref\nunions; empty falls back to HEAD). `installHook` upgrades a stale cledger block\nin place — without that, hook changes only ever reach fresh repos. Consuming\nstdin means anything chained *after* the block can't read it; safe in practice\nsince the block is appended last, and a user hook that drains stdin first just\ndegrades to HEAD scope.\n\n**Why per-branch *storage* / history-walking reads were rejected:** letting the\nremote tip hold only the current branch and having reads walk notes history\nwould break redaction outright — `redactEvent` squashes notes history so the\npre-redaction blob becomes unreachable, which only works because the tip is\nauthoritative. History-walking reads would resurrect every redacted value. Also\nbreaks `git notes show` interop and makes reads O(history). And it buys nothing\nthat union-into-remote-tip doesn't already give.","oldString":"**Known limitation:** the pre-push hook uses `</dev/null`, so it scopes by HEAD\nrather than the refs git is pushing. Pushing a branch you aren't on\nunder-sends (safe direction); next sync from that branch ships it.","originalFile":"---\nname: project-cledger-push-scope\ndescription: \"cledger 0.14.0 branch-scoped push — why the scope must resolve re_anchor, and why a filtered tree push silently clobbers\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295\n  modified: 2026-07-29T03:59:46.408Z\n---\n\nShipped 0.14.0 (on main). Push now carries only the anchors a read at that rev\nresolves to; storage unchanged.\n\n**The framing that unlocked it** (user's, 2026-07-27): three layers each need a\ngranularity — storage is per-commit, reads are per-branch, push was per-*ref*\ni.e. per-repo. Push was the only one out of step. Not a storage problem.\n\n**No mapping is persisted.** Reachability is recomputed from the DAG at push\ntime (`resolveAnchors`), same reason reads never stored it. Branch membership\nis derived; a stored copy needs maintaining through merge/rebase/rename/delete.\n\n**Two gotchas, each pinned by a test proven to fail against the wrong version:**\n\n1. *Scope must resolve `re_anchor`*, not just `git rev-list`. A squash merge\n   leaves conversations on anchors unreachable from the target; only mapping\n   events (anchored to the survivor) tie them back. Rev-list-only would push\n   the mappings and strand the events.\n2. *A scoped push must seed from the remote's tip and union into it.* A notes\n   ref is a snapshot of the whole database, not an append log — pushing a\n   filtered tree still fast-forwards while deleting every other branch's notes\n   from the remote's current view. Note the *unseeded* naive version is\n   harmless (non-FF rejection); it's the realistic \"filter my local ref\"\n   version that clobbers.\n\n**Side benefit:** the pre-push scan gate now only inspects in-scope events, so\nan out-of-scope finding no longer blocks unrelated pushes.\n\n**Known limitation:** the pre-push hook uses `</dev/null`, so it scopes by HEAD\nrather than the refs git is pushing. Pushing a branch you aren't on\nunder-sends (safe direction); next sync from that branch ships it.\n\n**Still open:** `readEvents`/`export` default to unscoped — the read half of\nthe same mismatch. Fix belongs in `readEvents`, since library consumers\n(intent-recall) never touch the CLI.\n\nSee [[project-cledger-worktree-gitdir]], [[project-ledger-ecosystem]].\n","replaceAll":false,"structuredPatch":[{"lines":["   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295","-  modified: 2026-07-29T03:59:46.408Z","+  modified: 2026-07-29T04:34:13.754Z"," ---"," "," Shipped 0.14.0 (on main). Push now carries only the anchors a read at that rev"],"newLines":7,"newStart":5,"oldLines":7,"oldStart":5},{"lines":[" **Side benefit:** the pre-push scan gate now only inspects in-scope events, so"," an out-of-scope finding no longer blocks unrelated pushes."," ","-**Known limitation:** the pre-push hook uses `</dev/null`, so it scopes by HEAD","-rather than the refs git is pushing. Pushing a branch you aren't on","-under-sends (safe direction); next sync from that branch ships it.","+**0.15.0:** the hook now passes git's pre-push stdin through, so scope follows","+the refs actually being pushed (local shas; deletions skipped; multi-ref","+unions; empty falls back to HEAD). `installHook` upgrades a stale cledger block","+in place — without that, hook changes only ever reach fresh repos. Consuming","+stdin means anything chained *after* the block can't read it; safe in practice","+since the block is appended last, and a user hook that drains stdin first just","+degrades to HEAD scope."," ","+**Why per-branch *storage* / history-walking reads were rejected:** letting the","+remote tip hold only the current branch and having reads walk notes history","+would break redaction outright — `redactEvent` squashes notes history so the","+pre-redaction blob becomes unreachable, which only works because the tip is","+authoritative. History-walking reads would resurrect every redacted value. Also","+breaks `git notes show` interop and makes reads O(history). And it buys nothing","+that union-into-remote-tip doesn't already give.","+"," **Still open:** `readEvents`/`export` default to unscoped — the read half of"," the same mismatch. Fix belongs in `readEvents`, since library consumers"," (intent-recall) never touch the CLI."],"newLines":22,"newStart":35,"oldLines":10,"oldStart":35}],"userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"8c5ac60a-1d2d-45ad-8835-f6db5135fb40","version":"2.1.220"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-07-29T04:35:29.260Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
