. The default probably needs to be terminal-aware, or CI opts in with `--report`.\n\nI did capture the part I think is the real insight — that the output should *name the failure mode* rather than just say \"don't look.\" An agent told *why* reading findings reproduces them will comply; a bare prohibition invites a workaround. Also worth noting masking the span (0.6.1) narrowed this loop but didn't close it: `keyword-assignment` trips on the *surrounding* credential-shaped context, which is still printed.\n\nAlso still on the list: `readEvents` defaulting to unscoped. That's the read half of the same mismatch you identified, and it belongs in `readEvents` rather than `export` precisely because intent-recall will never touch the CLI.\n\n`scripts/inspect-finding.py` is still untracked, and the design doc still references it.\n\nresult: cledger 0.14.0 on main (5f631f2) — push is now branch-scoped, resolving re_anchor mappings so squash-merged conversations still ship, and building on the remote's tip so a scoped push adds rather than clobbers; both properties pinned by tests proven to fail against the wrong implementations, and the scan gate now only inspects in-scope events.","type":"text"}],"diagnostics":null,"id":"msg_011CdVgQNX2aRYM9Rt8uiFgX","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":379,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":379,"cache_read_input_tokens":314963,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":2,"iterations":[{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":379,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":379,"cache_read_input_tokens":314963,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1680,"type":"message"}],"output_tokens":1680,"server_tool_use":{"web_fetch_requests":0,"web_search_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"}},"parentUuid":"a52905bf-3df5-4c59-b169-84b2cebcd9b